; Async.spawn/await run real threads on the legacy interpreter only; the EIR
; VM (the oracle) has no thread-backed closure execution and hard-errors with
; "unhandled effect: Async.spawn" (a loud, declared gap — Async.sleep alone
; IS ported and conforms). wasm rejects it too, conforming with the oracle's
; failure class.
; expect-fail: legacy — threads work there, so it prints 42 and exits 0
; while the VM oracle errors.
[fn main []
  [Async.sleep 1]
  [let f [Async.spawn [fn [] 21]]]
  [println [* 2 [Async.await f]]]]
